}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"02172ea1-1fca-4e9c-9b32-478782fbcc33"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The radar coordinates of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " are ",
 StyleBox["(d(v, b\:2081), \[Ellipsis], d(v, b\:2096))", "TI"],
 ". Every vertex gets its own coordinates exactly when the stations form a \
resolving set, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["ResolvingSetQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/ResolvingSetQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3477b41c-691a-48dc-a38a-78069af0521b"],
 "; the least number of stations that does is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["MetricDimension"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/MetricDimension", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8a499c58-6044-49ba-8228-474c7966aeb3"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d7cd3b5f-63b3-4e67-b814-8939dd48cee0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A station can be a set of vertices, given as a vertex list, a density or a \
walk graph. Its coordinate is the distance to the set, ",
 StyleBox["d(v, S) = min d(v, s)", "TI"],
 " over ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " in ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 ", or another function of the distances to its vertices."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0bbdd7dc-a3b3-493a-bd8c-6064c0202e4c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The point ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " can be a density; the result is then the list of the coordinates of its \
vertices."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c2679982-351a-4517-8b2f-dfe1cf7863c1"],

